{
  "name": "Android \u2014 Screen Load Timings",
  "tabs": [
    {
      "name": "Screen loads",
      "stylistic_components": [
        {
          "id": "t-h",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "Android \u2014 how long does each screen take to load?",
            "variant": "h2"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 3
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-p",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "Each span wraps a LaunchedEffect data load, and sits OUTSIDE the existing try/catch: inside, the catch would swallow the error and every span would record SUCCESS regardless of outcome. product_image_load uses Coil's onState callback (no loader rewrite needed, unlike iOS) and its chart excludes CANCELED, which Compose produces routinely when a row scrolls out of composition. No catalog_serialize span: Android fetches the catalog over the network rather than re-serializing locally.",
            "variant": "p"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 3,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 8
          }
        }
      ],
      "charts": [
        {
          "id": "c-0",
          "chart_component_layout": {
            "chart_id": {
              "workflow": {
                "workflow_id": "vokX",
